---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Collections — mgz-pkmn docs"
  description="Collections in mgz-pkmn: one-tap Own to track cards you have, organize into named collections, adjust quantities, and build smart collections from a saved rule."
  current="/docs/collections"
>
  <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sand-500 dark:text-sand-400">
    Your stuff
  </p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Collections
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-200">
    A collection is a bucket of cards you own and want to keep track of across
    lookups — "I have these." It's the owned half of your library, the mirror of a
    <a href="/docs/wishlists" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">wishlist</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Own a card, one tap
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Every card carries a one-tap <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Own</strong>
    action, the same everywhere — Search, Browse, Swipe, detail view. It drops the
    card into your default collection, <em>My collection</em>, made the first time
    you use it; tap again to remove. Use <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Add to a list…</strong>
    in a card's detail view to file it into a specific collection instead, with an
    inline "New collection…" option.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Collections show up in the <a href="/docs/binders" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Binders</a>
    tab of your <a href="/docs/backpack" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Backpack</a>
    with an <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Owned</strong> badge.
    Open one to adjust how many copies you have — the stepper floors at one, so a
    card never quietly disappears from the list by hitting zero. Delete a whole
    collection from its Backpack row's two-step trash control.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Smart collections
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    A smart collection isn't a hand-picked list — it's a <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">saved rule</strong>
    over your cards. Define a predicate once and its membership keeps up with your
    matching cards automatically, so "every Charizard I own" or "everything from
    Surging Sparks" stays current without re-curating it. You'll spot them by the
    sparkle marker in the Binders tab.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-palm-300 bg-palm-50 p-5 dark:border-sun-300/40 dark:bg-sun-300/5">
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-600 dark:text-sand-200">
      Want to see what your owned cards add up to? The Backpack's
      <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">collection insights</strong>
      give you a quick read across everything you own.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
